  "english_paragraphs": [
    "A little girl was left out of the choir by her teacher, so she sat alone in the park, crying sadly. After a while, she began to sing softly.",
    "“You sing beautifully!” a voice said. “Thank you, child. You’ve made my afternoon a lovely one.” The speaker was an old man, who walked away after saying this. The next day, he was sitting in the same spot, listening to the little girl sing with a kind smile on his face…",
    "Many years later, the little girl became a famous singer, but she never forgot the kind old man. When she went to find him and thank him, she learned that he had passed away."
  ],
  "english_full": "A little girl was left out of the choir by her teacher, so she sat alone in the park, crying sadly. After a while, she began to sing softly.\n\n“You sing beautifully!” a voice said. “Thank you, child. You’ve made my afternoon a lovely one.” The speaker was an old man, who walked away after saying this. The next day, he was sitting in the same spot, listening to the little girl sing with a kind smile on his face…\n\nMany years later, the little girl became a famous singer, but she never forgot the kind old man. When she went to find him and thank him, she learned that he had passed away.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "Немно́го́е́ де́вочка остала́сь вне хора́ у сво́егo наста́вника, поэ́тому она сиде́ла одна́ в парке́, гру́стно плача́. По́сле не́которого вре́мени она нача́ла ти́хо пе́ть.",
    "«Ты по́ешь краси́во!» — ска́зал го́лос. «Спаси́бо, ребёнок. Ты сдела́ла моё пополу́дни́ прекрасным.» Говоря́щий был пожило́й челове́к, кото́рый у́шёл прочь после́ того, как ска́зал это. На сле́дующий день он нахо́дился у то́т же места́, слушая́, как де́вочка пе́ла с доброй улы́бкой на лицe... ",
    "Мно́гие го́ды спустя́, де́вочка стала изве́стной певи́цей, но она никогда́ не забыла́ доброго старика́. Когда́ она пoшла́ найти́ его́ и благодари́ть, она узнала́, что он перешёл на́ ту сто́рону."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Nemońogoé dévotchka ostalás' vne khorá u svóego nast́avnika, póetomu ona sidéla odná v parké, grústno plachá. Pósle nékotorogo vremeńi ona nachalá tíkho pét'.",
    "«Ty póesh' kraśivo!» — skázal gólos. «Spaśibo, rébenok. Ty sdelála moё popolúdne prekraśnym.» Govoryáshchiy byl pozhilóy chelovéq, kotorý úsh'yot próch' poslé togo, kak skázal éto. Na sléduyushchiy deń on nakhod́ilsya u tót zhɪ mestá, slushayá, kak dévotchka péla s dóbroy ulýbkoy na liteŕe...",
    "Mnógie gódy spútya, dévotchka stala izvéstnoy pev́itséy, no ona nikogdá ne zabúdalá dóbrogo stariká. Kogdá ona pośhla náytí yégo i blagodarít', ona uználá, chto on pereshó̄l ná tu storónu."
  ],
